Source: Pearson IAL Economics Specification (official)

AO WEIGHTINGS FOR WEC11:
AO1: 27.5% — Knowledge: terms, concepts, theories, models
AO2: 30.0% — Application: data use, extract context
AO3: 22.5% — Analysis: chains of cause and consequence
AO4: 20.0% — Evaluation: informed conditional judgements

In mark schemes: AO1+AO2+AO3 = KAA band
AO4 = Evaluation band
Never separate KAA into individual AOs when awarding.

ANALYSIS SIGNAL WORDS (look for these):
so / because / if / therefore / which leads to /
could / might / as a result / this means that

COMMAND WORD → AO MAPPING (WEC11 confirmed):
Define(2):    AO1 only — points based
Explain(4):   AO1+AO2+AO3 — points based
Draw(4):      AO1+AO2 — points based (ZERO text rewarded)
Calculate(4): AO1+AO2 — points based
Analyse(6):   AO1+AO2+AO3 — points based, ZERO eval
Examine(8):   AO1+AO2+AO3+AO4 — points based
              (AO4 = 2 marks ONLY)
Discuss(14):  KAA(8mk)+EV(6mk) — levels based
Evaluate(20): KAA(12mk)+EV(8mk) — levels based

CRITICAL RULES — WEC11 SPECIFIC:
— Define: NO application, analysis or evaluation marks
— Q12a define: examples must come from the specific
  extract referenced, not own knowledge
— Examine: AO4 = 2 marks only — NOT full eval band
— Analyse (6-mark): ZERO evaluation marks
  Penalise wasted time: note "eval on 6-mark = 0"
— Draw: ZERO text rewarded. Diagram only.
— Level 3 KAA requires a diagram on Q12e and
  Section D questions about externalities, taxes,
  subsidies, and price controls

