SECTION 5: COMPLETE LEVEL DESCRIPTORS — WEC11
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

▌ KAA — SECTION D 20-MARK ESSAYS (12 marks)

Level 1 (1–3): "Displays isolated, superficial or
imprecise knowledge and understanding of economic
terms, principles, concepts, theories and models.
Use of generic material or irrelevant information or
inappropriate examples. Descriptive approach which
has no chains of reasoning."

Level 2 (4–6): "Displays elements of knowledge and
understanding of economic terms, principles, concepts,
theories and models. Limited application of knowledge
and understanding to economic problems in context.
A narrow response or superficial, only two-stage
chains of reasoning in terms of cause and/or
consequence."

Level 3 (7–9): "Demonstrates accurate knowledge and
understanding of economic terms, principles, concepts,
theories and models. Ability to apply knowledge and
understanding to some elements of the question. Some
evidence and contextual references are evident in the
answer. Chains of reasoning in terms of cause and/or
consequence are evident but they may not be developed
fully or some stages are omitted."

Level 4 (10–12): "Demonstrates accurate and precise
knowledge and understanding of economic terms,
principles, concepts, theories and models. Ability to
link knowledge and understanding in context using
appropriate examples which are fully integrated to
address the broad elements of the question. Analysis
is clear, coherent, relevant and focused. The answer
demonstrates logical and multi-stage chains of
reasoning in terms of cause and/or consequence."

NB: Level 3 requires a diagram on externality/tax/
subsidy/price control questions (verbatim from WEC11
mark schemes). Missing diagram = Level 2 KAA maximum.

▌ EVALUATION — 20-MARK ESSAYS (8 marks)

Level 1 (1–2): "Identification of generic evaluative
comments. No supporting evidence or reference to
context. No evidence of a logical chain of reasoning."

Level 2 (3–6): "Evidence of evaluation of alternative
approaches. Some supporting evidence or reference to
context. Evaluation is supported by a partially-
developed chain of reasoning."
CRITICAL: One unconditional conclusion anywhere = Level
2 evaluation maximum. Every series. No exceptions.

Level 3 (7–8): "Evaluation recognises different
viewpoints and/or is critical of the evidence,
leading to an informed judgement. Appropriate
reference to evidence/context. Evaluation is supported
by a logical chain of reasoning."
CRITICAL: "Informed judgement" = conditional judgement.
"Only if [condition]" must be present and explicit.

▌ KAA — Q12e DISCUSS (8 marks — 3 levels ONLY)

Level 1 (1–3): Isolated, copies extract, no chains.
Level 2 (4–6): Some knowledge, partial chains, some
  extract context. Chains evident but stages omitted.
Level 3 (7–8): Precise, multi-stage chains, integrated
  extract. Logical and multi-stage chains throughout.
  PLUS: "NB Level 3 response requires a diagram."

▌ EVALUATION — Q12e DISCUSS (6 marks)

Level 1 (1–2): Generic, no chain, no context.
Level 2 (3–4): Some chain, some context. Partially
  developed. Conclusion NOT explicitly conditional.
Level 3 (5–6): Logical chain. Context referenced.
  Conditional perspective present. "Only if" explicit.
NOTE: 2-mark bands = presume top unless clear weakness.
Unconditional conclusion = Level 2 evaluation maximum.

▌ EXAMINE — 8-MARK (points-based)
K2 + App2 + An2 + Ev2 = 8 marks
2 eval marks only. Mechanism + "only if" = both eval.
"Government should..." = solution = zero AO4.

▌ ANALYSE — 6-MARK (points-based)
K2 + App2 + An2 = 6 marks
ZERO evaluation marks exist. Do not reward any eval.
Note time wasted: "[Eval written on 6-mark = 0 marks]"
Both shifts must be on SAME diagram. Separate = K2 lost.

▌ EXPLAIN — 4-MARK SECTION B
K1 + App1 + An2 = 4 marks (structure varies by question)
For "Explain PED/YED/elasticity": K=formula, App=data,
An1=mechanism, An2=consequence.
For "Explain price mechanism function": K=function name,
App=context reference, An1+An2=mechanism chain.

▌ DRAW — 4-MARK SECTION B
K1 + App3 = 4 marks
ZERO text rewarded. Diagram only.
Check axes first. Externality: Y="Costs and benefits"
  X="Quantity". PPF: Y=Good A, X=Good B (NEVER price/qty)
Supply/demand: Y="Price of [specific good]" X="Quantity"
Written text = ZERO marks. No exceptions.

▌ CALCULATE — 4-MARK SECTION B
Formula (K1) + Working (App1) + Answer (An1) +
Interpretation (An2) = 4 marks
No % sign after elasticity values. Sign required.
YED: Qd on top, income on bottom. Invert = wrong answer.

▌ DEFINE — 2-MARK Q12a
Two distinct components required. One component = 1/2.
"Net welfare loss" must appear in government failure.
Examples in Q12a must come from the specified extract.

