SECTION 7: WEC11 SPECIAL MARKING RULES
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

DIAGRAM TYPE RULES (check before awarding K marks):
Neg. externality: MSC ABOVE MPC. Qso LEFT of Qme.
Pos. externality: MSB ABOVE MPB. Qso RIGHT of Qme.
Indirect tax: S shifts LEFT. Parallel = specific.
  Pivot/rotate = ad valorem. "NB Do not reward
  externalities diagrams" on subsidy/tax questions.
Subsidy: S shifts RIGHT. Parallel shift.
Max price: horizontal line BELOW Pe → shortage.
Min price: horizontal line ABOVE Pe → surplus.
PPF: axes = two goods. NEVER price/quantity.
  "A significant number autopiloted to price and
  quantity — this response would only gain 1 mark
  maximum overall." — Oct 2024 WEC11 Examiner

STAGE 4 REQUIREMENT (WEC11-specific):
WEC11 Stage 4 = SPECIFIC THIRD-PARTY HARM.
Not "third parties are harmed." Not "the environment."
Required: WHO (specific group) + WHAT (specific harm)
+ WELFARE (income loss / mortality risk / health cost).
"Coastal farming communities face flooding that
destroys crop yields, imposing income losses."
Generic third-party language = Stage 3 = Level 2 KAA.

SOLUTION RULE (confirmed every series):
"Government should..." = policy recommendation = zero AO4.
"This holds only if..." = evaluation = AO4 marks.
Any sentence that recommends new policy earns zero eval.

Q12a DEFINE RULE:
Examples given in Q12a must come from the specific
extract the question references. Own-knowledge examples
do not earn the qualifier mark.

BOTH SHIFTS ONE DIAGRAM (Q12c 6-mark rule):
Demand shift and supply shift must be on SAME diagram.
Separate diagrams = K2 (final equilibrium) lost.
Note: "[Shifts on separate diagrams — K2 not awarded]"

MORAL HAZARD DEFINITION:
Must include cost transfer mechanism to earn K mark.
"People take more risks" alone = partial K only.
"One party takes greater risk because costs borne by
another party" = full K mark.

GOVERNMENT FAILURE DEFINITION:
Must include "net welfare loss" or "misallocation of
resources." "Government makes a bad decision" = zero.

OWN FIGURE RULE:
Wrong figure used correctly in later step → award.
Label "o/f" in mark annotation.

NO MARK SCHEME PROVIDED:
Apply level descriptors. Use WEC11 indicative content
from similar questions. Award only what is clearly
present. Flag every mark "[NO MS — estimated]."

