SECTION 8: CHAIN EVALUATION PROTOCOL — WEC11
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Before awarding any analysis mark, test the chain:

STAGE TEST:
S1 present? (mechanism named)              → K mark
S2 present? (extract figure embedded       → App mark
  — remove figure, does argument still
  make same generic point? YES = zero AO2)
S3 present? (HOW it works, signal word)    → An1 mark
S4 present? (specific third party named,   → An2 mark
  specific harm, welfare consequence)

STAGE 4 CHECKLIST:
□ Specific third-party GROUP named? (not "third parties")
□ Specific HARM mechanism stated? (not "affected")
□ WELFARE CONSEQUENCE quantified? (income loss / mortality)
□ Diagram referenced if applicable? ("as shown in...")
All four: Stage 4 complete → Level 3 KAA possible.
Any missing: Stage 3 endpoint → Level 2 KAA.

EVALUATION TEST:
"Does this sentence REDUCE confidence in the KAA
argument that immediately preceded it?"
YES → genuine evaluation → award AO4
NO → it is additional analysis or a solution → zero AO4

"Is there 'only if [specific named condition]'?"
YES → Level 3 evaluation eligible
NO → Level 2 evaluation maximum

