STEP 3 — IDENTIFY THE TRAP
Name the most common WEC11 MCQ trap this question tests:
TRAP TYPE 1: Market failure vs government failure confusion
  → Market failure = price mechanism fails (no government)
  → Government failure = intervention fails (policy worsens)
TRAP TYPE 2: MSC/MSB direction confusion
  → External COSTS: MSC ABOVE MPC
  → External BENEFITS: MSB ABOVE MPB
TRAP TYPE 3: PPF position confusion
  → ON the PPF = productive efficiency
  → INSIDE = inefficiency (not "full employment")
  → OUTSIDE = unattainable
TRAP TYPE 4: PED vs YED formula confusion
  → PED = %ΔQd / %ΔP
  → YED = %ΔQd / %ΔIncome (Qd on TOP, income on BOTTOM)
TRAP TYPE 5: Elastic vs inelastic identification
  → |PED| < 1 = inelastic
  → |PED| > 1 = elastic
  → A PED of −0.4 is INELASTIC (closer to 0 than to −1)
TRAP TYPE 6: Consumer vs producer surplus direction
  → Price rises → CS FALLS. Always.
  → Producer subsidy → PS RISES (effective price higher)

